# WEFT: black key 11 (key 25) twice on WEFT PATCH or WEFT BLOCK unpatches the block: its own cords and the
# cords that read it come off; the block and the rest of the patch stay. PING SWITCH: 1 TICK, 2 RING (A 1),
# 3 RING (A 1), 4 STRING, 5 SAT (A 4), 6 SW 4>1 (A 2, B 1) ...
wait 300
kind 1 6
wpreset 1 17
tap EDIT
wait 50
turn SELECT 2
wait 100
expect page WEFT PATCH
turn K1 1
wait 100
# once: only asks
tapkey 25
wait 100
expect wsrc 1 2 1
expect wsrc 1 6 2
shot weft_unpatch_ask.png
wait 400
tapkey 25
wait 100
expect wsrc 1 2 0
expect wsrc 1 6 0
expect wsrc 1 3 1
expect wtype 1 2 25
shot weft_unpatch.png
wait 3000
# on WEFT BLOCK: block 1 (the TICK): the RING on 3 and the switch's B were reading it
turn K1 -1
wait 100
turn SELECT 1
wait 100
expect page WEFT BLOCK
shot weft_unpatch_blk.png
tapkey 25
wait 400
tapkey 25
wait 100
expect wsrc 1 3 0
expect wsrcb 1 6 0
expect wtype 1 1 24
